<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14056" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποτῑμ-άω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fail to honour, slight,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Merc.
				35
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				103
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.1389i
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				i33
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be disfranchised,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phleg.
				<u>Olymp.Fr.</u>
				14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>value,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ χρήματα,</span> of the owner, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				18.1.1
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, of the valuer, ibid., cf. <i><span class="en">
				17.13.5
			</span></i>; <i>fix a price by valuation,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίμνεως ἀποτιμησάμενοι</span>
			<i>having fixed their price</i> at two minae a head, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.77
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πολλοῦ αἰσχροὶ εἶναι</span>
			<i>value it</i> at a high price (i.e. to offer a great deal)
				<i>that they may not</i> be ugly, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				37
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be valued,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλειόνων χρημάτων</span> Catalog. ap.
				<i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.106
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>measure,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέτρον γῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					5.1.21
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> as law-term,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> in 
				Act.
			, <i>mortgage</i> a property, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				30.28
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				41.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, of the property, <i>to be pledged</i> or
				<i>mortgaged,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				30.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὶ εἰς προῖκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(7).57
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Amorgos</span>), cf. ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.1138
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
